{{Quote|I think we're on farmland. And where there's a farm, there's usually a farmer. Let's find his homestead.|Jesse|<ref name="Deserter" />}}
'''Lawquane's Farm''' was a [[farm]] owned by the [[Lawquane family|Lawquanes]] located on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] of [[Saleucami]] within the world's wetland region. After he deserted the [[Grand Army of the Republic]],<ref name="Deserter" /> the [[clone trooper]] [[Cut Lawquane]], his wife [[Suu Lawquane]], and his adopted children [[Shaeeah Lawquane]] and [[Jek Lawquane]], lived on the farm until they left Saleucami shortly after the [[Proclamation of the New Order|rise]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Cut and Run">{{TBB|Cut and Run}}</ref>

The farm comprised of at least two fields with a perimeter fence that deterred predators,<ref name="Cut and Run" /> the main house, which was two stories tall, as well as a barn complete with stables for [[eopie]]s. The clone troopers [[Rex]], [[Jesse]], and [[Hardcase]] encountered the farm during the [[Battle of Saleucami]], although they did not report Cut as a deserter and left the location of the farm a secret.<ref name="Deserter" /> [[Clone Force 99]] was also aware of the farm. After Clone Force 99 decided to leave Imperial service, they and their new companion [[Omega]] visited the farm to visit Lawquane. As the family was deciding to leave Saleucami due to the growing Imperial presence, the clones helped the family depart the planet.<ref name="Cut and Run" />

